Li). However, the MOFs-based membranes of zeolite imidazolium skeleton (ZIF-7) effectively prevent BP-Li transmission to the side of cathode (Figs. 12(b)–12(e)) [106]. Electrochemical performance of organic \(\mathrm{O}_{2}\) batteries based on BP-Li anode at different rates shows that the stable discharge plateau and charging plateau at \(\sim2.45\) and \(\sim2.75\;\mathrm{V}\) at low current density, respectively. A high current density of \(4,000\ \mathrm{mA{\cdot}g^{-1}}\) and a high reversible specific capacity of \(2,000\,\mathrm{\mAh{\cdot}g^{-1}}\) can be achieve with 100 cycles (Fig. 12(f)).MOFs have adjustable pore channels and open metal sites that facilitate mass transfer, \(\mathrm{O}_{2}\) enrichment and ORR/OER catalytic processes. In addition, the periodic structure and chemical stability of MOFs-based catalysts are also ideal choices for the \(\mathrm{Li}{-}\mathrm{O}_{2}\) batteries.
